---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page
	title="About · nonoise"
	description="About nonoise studio and the person behind it."
>
	<section class="about-page">
		<header class="about-intro">
			<h1>About</h1>
            <div class="about-photo">
                <img
                    src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50365584?v=4&size=600"
                    alt="That's me!"
                />
            </div>
			<p class="lead">
				I like understanding how things work, taking them apart, and
				figuring out how they could work better.
			</p>
		</header>

		<div class="about-content">
			<p>
				I'm Thomas. I'm an
				<span class="keyword">engineer</span> by training, with a
				background in <span class="keyword">Urbanism</span> and
				<span class="keyword">Industrial Design</span>.
			</p>

			<p>
				I've always been interested in how things fit together. Systems,
				objects, organisations, cities, businesses. I'll happily pull
				something apart just to understand why it works the way it does.
			</p>

			<p>
				That curiosity eventually found its way into
				<span class="keyword">data and digital tools</span>. Data is
				particularly interesting because it lets you look underneath the
				surface. You can see patterns, test assumptions, find
				vulnerabilities and discover things that aren't immediately
				obvious.
			</p>

			<p>
				But I also like
				<span class="keyword">design</span>. Not just making things look
				good, but thinking about what something should be, why it should
				work, and how people will actually use it.
			</p>

			<p>
				That kind of conceptual design is surprisingly close to
				<span class="keyword">business modelling</span>. Understand the
				world around you, spot an opportunity, and figure out how you
				could build something around it that actually works.
			</p>

            <h2>Why nonoise?</h2>

            <p>
                As a curious person, driven to understand how things work, I like to
                get close to the problem. I want to understand what is really going
                on, and what would make it better. That means asking questions,
                looking at the details, and being willing to rethink the obvious
                answer.
            </p>

            <p>
                In that process, I like to focus on what actually matters.
                <span class="keyword">Cut through the crap.</span>
                Strip away the unnecessary. Get to the point.
            </p>

            <p>
                I'm quite happy to <span class="keyword">question things, challenge assumptions and speak up</span>
                when I think something could be better. Not because I always have the
                right answer, but because not questioning it
                is rarely going to make it better.
            </p>

            <p>
                For me, that's about cutting through the noise. Removing the
                unnecessary, finding what actually matters, and focusing on what is
                useful.
            </p>

            <p>
                <span class="slogan">nonoise no nonsense.</span>
            </p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Page>


<style>
	.about-page {
		max-width: 48rem;
	}

	.about-intro {
		margin-bottom: 6rem;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 14rem;
		grid-template-areas:
			"title photo"
			"lead photo";
		column-gap: 3rem;
		row-gap: 1.5rem;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.about-intro h1 {
		grid-area: title;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-intro .lead {
		grid-area: lead;
	}

	.about-photo {
		grid-area: photo;
		width: 100%;
		aspect-ratio: 1;
		border-radius: 50%;
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.about-photo img {
		width: 100%;
		height: 100%;
		object-fit: cover;
		display: block;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		font-family: var(--font-bitcount, monospace);
		font-weight: 400;
	}

	.lead {
		max-width: 42rem;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.25rem);
		line-height: 1.25;
	}

	.about-content {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.about-content p {
		margin: 0 0 1.75rem;
	}

	.keyword {
		color: var(--electric);
	}

	.slogan {
		font-family: var(--font-bitcount, monospace);
		font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
		line-height: 1.25;
		color: var(--electric);
		text-align: center;
		display: block;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 5rem 0 1.5rem;
		font-family: var(--font-bitcount, monospace);
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1;
		color: var(--electric);
	}

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.about-intro {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 6rem;
			grid-template-areas:
				"title photo"
				"lead lead";
			column-gap: 1.25rem;
			row-gap: 1.5rem;
			margin-bottom: 4rem;
		}

		.about-photo {
			width: 6rem;
			align-self: center;
		}
	}
</style>